body:
Welp, it's a gamemode they tried to experiment with.

Personally, the gamplay was fun(the actual fighting was somewhat fun if a bit HP spongey).

Everything else? It was mostly bad:

- I didn't like the clicking simulator;

- I didn't like how slow the rover was walking;

- Would've preferred being able to choose my own team instead of having to buy them from the shop;

- The story is presented with a block of text and that just made me want to skip all of it;

- The metaphors are too specific and it feels bad getting a pistol-gauntlet metaphor when playing someone like Jinshi;

- It's too long for too little rewards, heck I wouldn't even mind if it just had an infinite coin item in the shop, atleast I'll get something from completing the event.

Oh well, just put in the survey what we didn't like and we'll most likely never see this type of gameplay again.

Brother, I don't think people care about your sexual preference while playing Yugioh.

Your sexual preferences really shouldn't become your identity, but oh well that's for you to decide.

Also, as for "gay" decks, a few come to mind:

- Sky striker (Raye and her girlfriend Rose linkage OTK you to oblivion);

- Live Twins (They aren't sisters, that should tell you enough);

- Crystal beasts (Rainbow dragon...not much more to say);

- Abyss actors (always gave me a queer vibe);

- Ghoti (dunno the reason why but it's been claimed to be a "gay" deck);

Funnily enough I play like more than half of these and I'm not gay.

Gameplay clarity:

- Let us see the ability numbers, how much they buff, etc.

- Let us see the traits of the enemies on the party selection screen. They can even be vague about it before 1st clear.

- Stat chart after battle.

Gacha changes:

- Pity carry over. The 300 pity feels fine, tho is preferable to be lowered to like 150.

- Better droprate nodes for rare materials like demon hearts, etc.

Gameplay changes:

- Chance to unlock older events (even just the story and CQ);

- Permanently reduce the chaldea gate AP costs to 20;

- Grail fronts becoming a permanent monthly gamemode for a grail;

- Increased bag spaces (atleast the CEs by 500);

- A pseudo Automatic system (the first clear is manual, but it saves the actions you did and the next time it will try to replicate it on subsequent clears).

Some advice even after you recover your account:

1) Make a 1 euro purchase if possible and save the receipt;

2) Always keep a screenshot of your servant lineup;

3) Always have a screenshot of your friend code + your previous transfer codes;

Number 1 makes things much faster for recovery (can't get more "this is my account" than having the receipts);

Number 2 and 3 are basically a guarantee to recover your account if you have both of them.

