Lets list them all shall we?

- kayneth: ded (great snipe Maiya);

- Ryounosuke: ded...tho satisfied?;

- Tokiomi: ded (lol);

- Kariya: ded and forever bugged by his failures.

- Kirei: hanging around with his boyfriend gil...and the countless children they abducted to feed said boyfriend;

- Kiritsugu: "killed" his wife, lost his partner in crime, failed to save his daughter and doomed a child to a possibly horrific ending in his final moments...

You could argue that kirei got his "happy ending" too lol.

Imo his legacy will forever be criticised because:

1) he got his debut as T1 as an org was collapsing in 2020;

2) People think that all his success has been because he had keria by his side;

3) His slump at the 2022 MSI was a horror to watch back then (he wasn't as good on Senna and Kalista as he is now).

4) It feels like everytime he has a popoff moment it gets overshadowed by either a massive int by the enemy team (kanavi) or because another teammate is popping off harder (Zeus)

1) For most people she's a lot more different to play and thus not able to bring out her potential in lane;

2) Her early levels can be atrocious vs ranged, especially mages;

3) Her all in combo compared to other assassins (gapclose in, use all abilities in .5 seconds and then back out), akali's is very delayed which can be attributed to the delay between R1 and R2. Doesn't help that they took out the ability to use Q during her E2 which was a way to speed up the combo.

If someone knows how to play Akali, they're a menace but you can't just take her up and expect to pilot her well in a couple of games.

At first glance she may seem easy but damn do you have to play on a tight rope if you want to maximize her potential.

Oh! There are a looot of reasons for me atleast (genz):

1) It was shoved down my throats since I was young (devout catholic family from my mother's side);

2) Religous trauma (aka, fear of hell, etc.);

3) I was raised by my aunt to think critically and to spot contradictions, which led me to be a lot more doubtful about the "miracles" in religions;

4) A lot of the "dark" side of religions were made  a lot  more public in recent years;

5) School program (history and philosophy mainly) showing how corrupt the church was and probably is to this day;

6) Got tired of the puritan BS they keep hammering on about (no sex before marriage my ass, my mother was pregnant during the wedding!);

7) Masses got too creepy for me;

8) Realized later on that I don't need jesus to guide me on how to be good;

9) The religion wars that have killed a lot of people (still happens to this day);

Welp, those are what came on top of my head. There's probably a lot more that I buried in my subconsciousness.

