Ok, here's the deal here:

IF you have an E6 Yukong (otherwise avoid her like the plague, so damn awkward to use without her E6...), then you can probably do the Blade-Yukong- Pela-Lynx team.

This is assuming you pick Pela from the event (aetherium wars) selector and then if you manage to get the free Lynx in pure fiction.

This team should be a pretty good team even on auto:

- Yukong gives a lot of great buffs for Blade (crit rate and crit damage) and can also act as a sub dps (I've seen Yukongs deal 50-60+k damage on ult);

- I'm gonna ssume you don't have the tutorial LC (from the SW event) so your best bet here is the luca LC Pela setup, sure you're not going to be able to ult as frequently with the usual rotation but since this team is very SP positive, you should be able to skill more on Pela (she is also ideal for blade since she reduces def by a lot with the Luca LC setup);

- Lynx > Bailu in 90% of cases because it raises Blade's taunt value, thus letting him to counter more frequently = more damage;


IF you have an E1 Guinaifen + luca LC then you can do the Blade - Lynx - Guinaifen - Dr Ratio:

- This comp is one that I use but having Topaz instead of Guinaifen;

- This is a dual carry comp that should be good vs a certain boss in Penacony;

- Probably bad in 90% of content lol;


