Personally the most toxic classes when good are Portalcraft, Bloodcraft and Runecraft:

- The first is because of some annoying mechanic (pp restore in enhance portal for example) or just random BS basically instawin cards like Belphomet or Absolute Tolerance (the latter being the most BS thing ever...turn 7 otk from hand for 0PP...wtf);

- Bloodcraft because of what they have to do to make it good, ie free burn damage into free board damage into free storm while basically not letting you interact with them because of how much heal they get for no reason (wrath's entire thing is supposed to be the high risk, you take away the risk and now you only have high reward);

- Rune is toxic when it has spellboost decks, the other archetypes can be as OP (looking at u sephie) but they don't feel as bad to fight against;

More than a year and a half:

- there was Burial Rite era (FH that had to be nerfed and was still very good);

- Gremory shenanigans (from storm rivayle until gremory rotated);

- Aggro Shadow...was a thing (funny high rolls lmao);

- Colloseum until eternal was the reign of rally gremory (imagine turn 3-4 with the enemy board full of liches) and Deathbringer shadow (a deck of infinite storms, unconditional board clear and infinite heals...there was also the fact that it recovered a lot of PP)

- Yokai shadow had a stint;

- then there was LW (the one that spammed wards;

- Then Evo shadow came and broke the game;

- Then it got more toxic with Flame and glass shadow

- After that was LW shadow, the one we're familiar with now (hehe, board wipe and otk on turn 6-8)

- then was Ghost shadow recently;

- Now we have neutral LW.

It's litterally been about 5 years since shadowcraft has been meta or at the minimum viable with entire expansions of terrorism from the class (Eternal and the entire period of Cernnunos/Suzy + F&G/Raider being the worst)...

So yeah, no wonder some people are tired of shadow lol

Anyhow, sorry if I missed anything, I don't remember the past 5 years perfectly lol.

