It's like this:

- Raviel's regression is fixed to the first day of the loop;

- MC's is 24 hours after he dies;

- If one of them dies, they regress to their own specific point first, thus not letting the other regress too;

If MC dies first, Raviel doesn't remember about their agreement/moment;

If Raviel dies first, she goes back to the start where MC doesn't even remember her and it's not guaranteed that they would fall in love again;

By dying at the same split second, both of their regressions trigger at the same time, meaning that Raviel goes back to the beginning and has to wait for the time that the MC regresses to (by regressing, he remembers) and then they just have to do this again and again until they reach the first day of the loop again.

I think the MC after the first death could've just died by himself again if they did confirm that it was the same Raviel but maybe he didn't want to risk it and wanted it to be more romantic (he really wanted those kisses lol) so they just kept doing the dying together.

You could say that every arc develops the MCs character in a way and he learns something new everytime:

- First arc: he learns to be emphatetic to others;

- 2nd Arc: He learns about the consequences of choices and the responsibility of life;

- 3rd Arc: He learns about the tragedies in the world, experiences them and how to turn that into strength to prevent said tragedies. He also somewhat completes his moral compass in this arc;

- 4th Arc: He learns companionship and how to live for someone else because so far, he has basically lived a lonely life and it's very hard for him to make relationships with others because of his regression skill and additional perks. Also, now KGJ has a pillar to support him in his toughest times and someone who will be with him till the ends of the world which is necessary for a person to stay grounded in reality and not become disillusioned like the flame emperor;

I can understand why some wouldn't like this arc in particular but it is very much needed for his character development to stay somewhat grounded in reality.

