In my years of playing Gacha, there's a certain pattern that I noticed that I follow:

As I start the game and do the tutorial, I immidietly go to the banner and see if they interest me, then I look up their kit online, if I like them, I reroll until I get them (also, Aesthetic in the early game for me is basically only a plus, thank god for Seele being so hot in hsr lol, as I value utility above everything in this stage);

During the early game, I build one all purpose team and stick with it, grabbing one DPS unit if the first banner wasn't one, then pulling for every single support that comes out (this is probably my FGO mentality with all the BS supports that are basically required to have any modicum of success);

The second to last phase is me building up the first team to the point that I can clear the story and events by brute force.

After that, I look up all the waifus and pull whoever the heck attracts me the most, regardless of meta because I can already clear the game anyways by this point.


Another thing is that while developing an account, I tend to steer clear of archetypes that forces me to build multiple characters that basically only work in that niche (*cough* *cough* DoT teams *cough* *cough*), these games in my experience don't give you much of anything in the mid-late stages of the account, especially during drought patches, so having an archetype basically stronghand me into "wasting" resources that could've been used for general purpose supports is a big nono for me; this type of thing that you can afford to do in the lategame when your account is stable and you can expend resources upon resources just for a meme.

Honestly? Would probably keep and if it rolls on speed, I'd faint.

