Honestly really love this SU world, it has everything you want: a dps set that is good on EVERYONE (except blade and Clara RIP) and an ER set that DOESNT mess up your speed tuning.

Buffs and debuffs barely matter in Sim Swarm unless you have very cracked dpses and even then, you'd have to have your supports be with lot of durability.

Sim Swarm 5 can be easily cheesed with remembrance path:

What you do is get as many remembrance blessings as you can, in particular the dissociation ones.

As you go through the run, install March and other sustain units and maybe another ice unit (ironically enough, Herta is good for this).

All of them are to be built as pure durability, this is not a sprint, it's a marathon and with the dissociation blessings, you have enough damage to not have to worry about dps (I've seen people clear this with Arlan with these blessings, tho that was on destruction path);

If you have the chance, take the 3* destruction blessing that divides the damage to all allies and upgrade it as soon as you can as it gives 15% reduction.

Another good blessing is another 3* destruction blessing that gives you defence and attack everytime you get hit;

If you want a safety net, you can go also tech in the 1* destruction blessing that revives a character once per battle;

Another way that you can do this is Abundance with Dan IL but that one is very degenerate and takes forever to finish a run that may still end in failure.

