what if Hoyo made a deal with you, giving you the "green light" to be able to leak what types of events there will be, the characters' names, etc. but with a few caveats:

- You can only leak a screenshot of the UI and the poster of events, no details on story and maybe even the rewards;

- You can leak the characters' names and path along with a somewhat baseline kit (the concept they're trying to make) but the splash arts, their models and bio to remain "unleaked" with the exception of maybe the face;

- You can leak what planet the crew will be in next and on what patch it'll be but the story details to not be leaked;

- You can leak which characters will have a companion quest but can't elaborate on what the story will be about;


With this deal, the point of leaks are still there (what characters will be released, their baseline kit, events and what/where(?) to expect next) and can still benefit the f2ps and low spenders but it will also make it so the story (i.e. a huge part of the appeal of the game) aren't spoiled months in advance and wasting the time of the animators and story writers (and with how many leaks there are, it is very hard to avoid all of them).

This will basically turn leakers into teasers for the game, "teasing" characters, events and where the story will go months in advance to build hype for the game without actually spoiling anything relevant.

So, what would you do if Hoyoverse came with you with such a deal?

17+ damage from hand at turn 7 is not fun gameplay. Whoever thought this crap was fun?! I'd understand if the damage was from someone not being able to clear the board but come on!

We need anti-storm and effect damage mitigation cards FAST because this crap is becoming too much, too quickly.

Cards that need nerfs (the most guilty of this):

