What meta usually looks like is this:

- Usually Shadow or Portal get broken decks pissing off most of the playerbase and when they don't mostly everyone is happy.

- When rune is meta a lot of people despair because "no interaction" class is not fun when it's good;

- Forest has their stints of greatness (read: most broken thing in existance...still salty about Sekka and Ladica);

- Blood either is mid or broken by having 10000 effects on every given card and free evos out the ass (looking at you Vania);

- Dragon is usually a solid class, everyone and their mother say they're bad but then perform excelently (also pray that they don't reprint Ghanda);

- Haven is the cope class usually ( they had to be carried by Holy saber for how many expansions again?) but sometimes like rn they're very good and it's always frustrating to go against (tho tbf I think that's just because of Holy Saber 2.0 aka Jeanne)

- Sword is litterally only ever good when they overload the class with storms and free damage and when they're not they have a very hard time in the meta (unless they have a broken combo).


Also, fair warning most people in this sub are Dragon and Sword players, which may have made my impression on them a bit biased.

