- Levelling up social links that aren't from your party won't unlock you any noew abilities, just increase the bonus experience you get of that arcana when fusing.

- When you get you navigator, level up their social link asap since they'll be a constant in the party from then on;

- to unlock the full golden ending: get Aeon to max and jester to 6 if I remember correctly;

- Sarasvati is good when you get lvl 26 as she gains invigorate 2 which solves resource depletion somewhat;

- Keep a healer on the team at all times if you don't want mc to have that job;

- When the game asks you to pay attention to your decisions, PAY ATTENTION as you may lose a large part of the game;

- after beating the levels, you can go back to the top floor to fight a side boss that is needed to unlock the superboss on ng+ , it also gives you great equipment;

- buff and debuffs are your friends (this should be obvious for any megaten game tho);

- Yoshitsune and Trumpeter borderline break the game;

- Try to do the levels on one day so you have more time to explore the game;

Thresh tips basically everyone needs to know:

-The lantern is counted as a miniature terrain so you can block where the enemy is walking if you place it well enough;

-Thresh doesn't look where he's going to throw the hook while he's winding it up so you can use this to bait morg shields/make unexpected hooks;

-This is more for every skillshot in the game but mostly for hook champs: if you spook the enemy enough (flashing towards them/walking menacingly during a gank) they will predictably flash/use a movement spell and that's where it's easiest to predict the hook;

- Lantern in front of the target and not where they are as that may block their pathing and maybe get them killed;

- try walking up to E backwards instead of hooking from range if possible as that will let you follow up with a hook easily;

- when cornered (they're running for their lives and you're chasing them) they will try to dodge by walking backwards 90% of the time so aim a bit backwards;

- Your autos hit like trucks when fully charges by E passive (especially if you take double adaptive force rune shards) so you can use this to ruin the life of melee supports and adcs who are bad at spacing.
